        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_58ad1d22_3803_4c95_a137_207cfebe242a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">a vector of discrete times</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_58ad1d22_3803_4c95_a137_207cfebe242a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">TimeVector</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3258329</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">For any electrolyte A_xB_y, the limiting molar conductivity is expressed as x times the limiting molar conductivity of A^{y+} and y times the limiting molar conductivity of B^{x-}.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molar_conductivity#Kohlrausch&apos;s_law_of_independent_migration_of_ions</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">proposed by Friedrich Kohlrausch between 1875-1879</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">valid for dilute solutions</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_598ae3d0_76e9_429c_a0e1_8694525cb574</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">KohlrauschsLaw</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">linear scan voltammetry with slow scan rate in which a dropping mercury electrode is used as the working electrode</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://doi.org/10.1515/pac-2018-0109</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">If the whole scan is performed on a single growing drop, the technique should be called single drop scan voltammetry. The term polarography in this context is discouraged.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">This is the oldest variant of polarographic techniques, introduced by Jaroslav Heyrovský (1890 – 1967).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Usually the drop time is between 1 and 5 s and the pseudo-steady-state wave-shaped dependence on potential is called a polarogram. If the limiting current is controlled by dif- fusion, it is expressed by the Ilkovich equation.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a0f3b6a_10b4_43a7_b0b6_4eb5c077980e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">DCPolarography</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a7a3028_db9e_4045_ab68_054c6afc91fc</IRI>
        <Literal>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q899494</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_5a7a3028_db9e_4045_ab68_054c6afc91fc</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">the rate of the chemical reaction is directly proportional to the product of the activities or concentrations of the reactants</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
