        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#AmperePerMetre</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en"> is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566  371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of &quot;magnetization&quot; in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</Literal>
