    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#Dalton</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">One dalton is defined as one twelfth of the mass of an unbound neutral atom of carbon-12 in its nuclear and electronic ground state.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#Dalton</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The unified atomic mass unit (symbol: μ) or dalton (symbol: Da) is a unit that is used for indicating mass on an atomic or molecular scale. It is defined as one twelfth of the rest mass of an unbound atom of carbon-12 in its nuclear and electronic ground state, and has a value of 1.660538782(83) × 10⁻²⁷ kg. One Da is approximately equal to the mass of one proton or one neutron. The CIPM have categorised it as a &quot;non-SI unit whose values in SI units must be obtained experimentally&quot;.

-- QUDT</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
