    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#Degree</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Degree is a measurement of plane angle, defined by representing a full rotation as 360 degrees.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#Degree</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A degree (in full, a degree of arc, arc degree, or arcdegree), usually denoted by ° (the degree symbol), is a measurement of plane angle, representing 1/360 of a full rotation; one degree is equivalent to  2π /360 rad, 0.017453 rad. It is not an SI unit, as the SI unit for angles is radian, but is an accepted SI unit.

-- QUDT</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2"/>
