    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">VIM defines measurand as a quantity intended to be measured. This is redundant in EMMO and correspond to Quantity.</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_bb49844b_45d7_4f0d_8cae_8e552cbc20d6"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measurand</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_bb49844b_45d7_4f0d_8cae_8e552cbc20d6"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">quantity</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">VIM defines a quantity as a &quot;property of a phenomenon, body, or substance, where the property has a magnitude that can be expressed as a number and a reference&quot;.

A quantity in EMMO is a property and therefore only addresses the first part of the VIM definition (that is a property of a phenomenon, body, or substance). The second part (that it can be expressed as a number and a reference) is syntactic and addressed by emmo:QuantityValue.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Measurand</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
