    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_12b2ec1e_fb89_468a_a51d_97c2a6db297c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ratio of the product of ion molality b and a correction factor γ to the molality b° of the same ion in a standard solution under standardized conditions: a = bγ / b°.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_12b2ec1e_fb89_468a_a51d_97c2a6db297c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Normally a standard solution is a solution of the ion at a molality of 1 mol/kg (exactly). Standardized conditions are normally 1013,25 hPa and 25 °C.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_12b2ec1e_fb89_468a_a51d_97c2a6db297c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The correction factor is called activity coefficient and it is determined experimentally. See ActivityCoefficient</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
