        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_251cfb4f_5c75_4778_91ed_6c8395212fd8</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The beauty of that girl.
The style of your clothing.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_251cfb4f_5c75_4778_91ed_6c8395212fd8</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The word subjective applies to property intrisically subjective or non-well defined. In general, when an black-box-like procedure is used for the definition of the property.

This happens due to e.g. the complexity of the object, the lack of a underlying model for the representation of the object, the non-well specified meaning of the property symbols.

A &apos;SubjectiveProperty&apos; cannot be used to univocally compare &apos;Object&apos;-s.

e.g. you cannot evaluate the beauty of a person on objective basis.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
