        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_40989212_4866_41c0_8a20_84fd39540f29</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">For the dissociation of a salt AmBn → mA + nB, the solubility product is KSP = am(A) ⋅ an(B), where a is ionic activity and m and n are the stoichiometric numbers.</Literal>
