    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_52211e5e_d767_4812_845e_eb6b402c476a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A &apos;Physical&apos; which is a tessellation of &apos;State&apos; temporal direct parts.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_52211e5e_d767_4812_845e_eb6b402c476a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">&apos;Existent&apos; is the EMMO class to be used for representing real world physical objects under a reductionistic perspective (i.e. objects come from the composition of sub-part objects, both in time and space). 

&apos;Existent&apos; class collects all individuals that stand for physical objects that can be structured in well defined temporal sub-parts called states, through the temporal direct parthood relation.

This class provides a first granularity hierarchy in time, and a way to axiomatize tessellation principles for a specific whole with a non-transitivity relation (direct parthood) that helps to retain the granularity levels.

e.g. a car, a supersaturated gas with nucleating nanoparticles, an atom that becomes ionized and then recombines with an electron.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_52211e5e_d767_4812_845e_eb6b402c476a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An &apos;Existent&apos; individual stands for a real world object for which the ontologist wants to provide univocal tessellation in time.

By definition, the tiles are represented by &apos;State&apos;-s individual.

Tiles are related to the &apos;Existent&apos; through temporal direct parthood, enforcing non-transitivity and inverse-functionality.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_52211e5e_d767_4812_845e_eb6b402c476a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Being hasTemporalDirectPart a proper parthood relation, there cannot be &apos;Existent&apos; made of a single &apos;State&apos;.

Moreover, due to inverse functionality, a &apos;State&apos; can be part of only one &apos;Existent&apos;, preventing overlapping between &apos;Existent&apos;-s.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">ex-sistere (latin): to stay (to persist through time) outside others of the same type (to be distinct from the rest).</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_52211e5e_d767_4812_845e_eb6b402c476a</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Existent</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
