        <Literal xml:lang="en">Ruby</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A relation between two holistic wholes that properly overlap, sharing one of their holistic parts.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A man and the process of building a house. 
The man is a whole that possesses an holistic temporal part which is an interval of six monts and represents a working period in his lifetime.
The process of building a house is a whole that possesses an holistic spatial part which is a builder.
The working period of the man and the builder participating the building process are the same individual, belonging both to a man lifetime and to a building holistic views.
In this sense, the man and the building process overcrosses. and the overlapping individual is represented differently in both holistic views.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">This relation is about two wholes that overlap, and whose intersection is an holistic part of both.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">hasHolisticOverlap</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
