        <Literal xml:lang="en">DefinedEdgeCutting</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:isDefinedBy"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/fr/#iso:std:iso-iec:2382:-1:ed-3:en</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8681074a_e225_4e38_b586_e85b0f43ce38</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">All or part of the programs, procedures, rules, and associated documentation of an information processing system.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:seeAlso"/>
            <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://www.linfo.org/program.html</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8681074a_e225_4e38_b586_e85b0f43ce38</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Software is usually used as a generic term for programs. However, in its broadest sense it can refer to all information (i.e., both programs and data) in electronic form and can provide a distinction from hardware, which refers to computers or other electronic systems on which software can exist and be use.
Here we explicitly include in the definition also all the data (e.g. source code, script files) that takes part to the building of the executable, are necessary to the execution of a program or that document it for the users.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From soft +‎ -ware, by contrast with hardware (“the computer itself”). Coined by Paul Niquette in 1953.</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8681074a_e225_4e38_b586_e85b0f43ce38</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Software</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A measurement unit symbol that do not have a metric prefix as a direct spatial part.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">NonPrefixedUnit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_869e6e4f_a9b5_4db8_a978_8ad050239933</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">PerThermalTransmittanceUnit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86a305d1_7644_48be_b84c_1f976679b904</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A device that is designed to participate to a manufacturing process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86a305d1_7644_48be_b84c_1f976679b904</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ManufacturingDevice</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An object that has been designed and manufactured for a particular purpose.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Car, tire, composite material.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin arte ‘by or using art’ + factum ‘something made’.</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Artifact</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin ingenium &quot;innate qualities, ability; inborn character,&quot; in Late Latin &quot;a war engine, battering ram&quot;; literally &quot;that which is inborn,&quot; from in- (&quot;in&quot;) + gignere (&quot;give birth, beget&quot;).</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Engineered</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From late Latin tangibilis, from tangere ‘to touch’.</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">TangibleProduct</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin manufacture: &quot;made by hand&quot;.</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ca9b93_1183_4b65_81b8_c0fcd3bba5ad</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ManufacturedProduct</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_86ffe1bb_d457_4948_9e39_35f363b9a9fe</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ElectricConductivityUnit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_873b0ab3_88e6_4054_b901_5531e01f14a4</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A quantity that is the result of a well-defined measurement procedure.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_873b0ab3_88e6_4054_b901_5531e01f14a4</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The specification of a measurand requires knowledge of the kind of quantity, description of the state of the phenomenon, body, or substance carrying the quantity, including any relevant component, and the chemical entities involved.

-- VIM</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_873b0ab3_88e6_4054_b901_5531e01f14a4</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">MeasuredProperty</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A spatial contact between two entities occurs when the two entities are in an interaction relation whose causal structure is a representation of the fundamental interactions between elementary particles (Feynman diagrams).
It means that if two entities are in contact, then there is at least a couple of elementary particles, one part of the first and one part of the second, interacting according to one of the fundamental interactions through virtual particles. This kind of connection is space-like (i.e. interconnecting force carrier particle is offshelf).
Contacts between two entities exclude the possibility of other causal relations that are not included in a fundamental space-like interaction.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An interaction that is the sum of direct causality relations between two entities that are interpretable as fundamental physical interactions.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Spatial contact is symmetric and irreflexive.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The contact relation is not an ordering relation since is symmetric.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">hasSpatiialnteractionWith</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8785be5a_2493_4b12_8f39_31907ab11748</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">contacts</Literal>
