        <Literal xml:lang="en">A logarithmic unit is a unit that can be used to express a quantity (physical or mathematical) on a logarithmic scale, that is, as being proportional to the value of a logarithm function applied to the ratio of the quantity and a reference quantity of the same type.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
