        <Literal xml:lang="en">A well defined physical entity, elementary or composite, usually treated as a singular unit, that is found at scales spanning from the elementary particles to molecules, as fundamental constituents of larger scale substances (as the etymology of &quot;particle&quot; suggests).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_a15cea10_9946_4d2b_95c5_cfc333fd2abb</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The scope of the physical particle definition goes from the elementary particles to molecules, as fundamental constituents of substances.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
