        <Literal xml:lang="en">A coded that makes use of an atomic symbol with respect to the code used to refer to the interaction.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Hardness is a subclass of properties.
Vickers hardness is a subclass of hardness that involves the procedures and instruments defined by the standard hardness test.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The name &quot;red&quot; which is atomic in the code made of the list of colors.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A property is atomic in the sense that is aimed to deliver one and one only aspect of the object according to one code, such as the color with one sign (e.g., black) or a quantitiative property (e.g., 1.4 kg).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin proprietas (“a peculiarity, one&apos;s peculiar nature or quality, right or fact of possession, property”), from proprius (“special, particular, one&apos;s own”).</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Property</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b803f122_4acb_4064_9d71_c1e5fd091fc9</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The class of individuals that stands for semiotic objects, i.e. objects that take part on a semiotic process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b803f122_4acb_4064_9d71_c1e5fd091fc9</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Semiotic subclasse are defined using Peirce&apos;s semiotic theory.

&quot;Namely, a sign is something, A, which brings something, B, its interpretant sign determined or created by it, into the same sort of correspondence with something, C, its object, as that in which itself stands to C.&quot; (Peirce 1902, NEM 4, 20–21).

The triadic elements:
- &apos;sign&apos;: the sign A (e.g. a name)
- &apos;interpretant&apos;: the sign B as the effects of the sign A on the interpreter (e.g. the mental concept of what a name means)
- &apos;object&apos;: the object C (e.g. the entity to which the sign A and B refer to)

This class includes also the &apos;interpeter&apos; i.e. the entity that connects the &apos;sign&apos; to the &apos;object&apos;</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b803f122_4acb_4064_9d71_c1e5fd091fc9</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">SemioticEntity</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b82d6a44_ea23_4b68_9b24_70f77deac955</IRI>
        <Literal>https://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/TotalIonization</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b82d6a44_ea23_4b68_9b24_70f77deac955</IRI>
        <Literal>https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q98690787</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_8de5d5bf_db1c_40ac_b698_095ba3b18578"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b82d6a44_ea23_4b68_9b24_70f77deac955</IRI>
        <Literal>10-59</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b82d6a44_ea23_4b68_9b24_70f77deac955</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Quotient of the total mean charge of all positive ions produced by an ionizing charged particle along its entire path and along the paths of any secondary charged particles, and the elementary charge.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b82d6a44_ea23_4b68_9b24_70f77deac955</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">TotalIonization</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b85e4738_500c_4e1b_bbe8_9e84190485d6</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An indirect cause is a relation between two entities that is mediated by a intermediate entity. In other words, there are no quantum parts of the causing entity that are direct cause of quantum parts of the caused entity.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b85e4738_500c_4e1b_bbe8_9e84190485d6</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A causal relation between the effected and the causing entities with intermediaries.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b85e4738_500c_4e1b_bbe8_9e84190485d6</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">isIndirectCauseOf</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
