        <Literal xml:lang="en">A pure number, typically the number of something.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_ba882f34_0d71_4e4f_9d92_0c076c633a2c</IRI>
        <Literal>1,
i,
π,
the number of protons in the nucleus of an atom</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_ba882f34_0d71_4e4f_9d92_0c076c633a2c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">According to the SI brochure counting does not automatically qualify a quantity as an amount of substance.

This quantity is used only to describe the outcome of a counting process, without regard of the type of entities.

There are also some quantities that cannot be described in terms of the seven base quantities of the SI, but have the nature of a count. Examples are a number of molecules, a number of cellular or biomolecular entities (for example copies of a particular nucleic acid sequence), or degeneracy in quantum mechanics. Counting quantities are also quantities with the associated unit one.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_ba882f34_0d71_4e4f_9d92_0c076c633a2c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">PureNumberQuantity</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_bafc17b5_9be4_4823_8bbe_ab4e90b6738c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process occurring with the active participation of an agent that drives the process according to a specific objective (intention).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_bafc17b5_9be4_4823_8bbe_ab4e90b6738c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Project</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin intentionem, derived from intendere (&quot;stretching out&quot;)</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_bafc17b5_9be4_4823_8bbe_ab4e90b6738c</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">IntentionalProcess</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
