        <Literal xml:lang="en">A cloud.
A picture.
A colour gradient on a wall.
A stain.
A mail.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ae6d8e_6b39_431f_8de4_ae4e357abc04</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Visual</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The most fundamental unity criterion for the definition of an structure is that:
- is made of at least two quantums (a structure is not a simple entity)
- all quantum parts form a causally connected graph</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The union of CausalPath and CausalSystem classes.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A self-connected composition of more than one quantum entities.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A causal structure expresses itself in time and space thanks to the underlying causality relations between its constituent quantum entities. It must at least provide two temporal parts.
The unity criterion beyond the definition of a causal structure (the most general concept of structure) is the existence of an undirected causal path between each of its parts.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25"/>
            <Literal xml:lang="en">From Latin causa (“reason, sake, cause”), and Medieval Latin obiectum (“object”, literally “thrown against”).</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">CausalObject</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
