    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84"/>
        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#Mole</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The mole, symbol mol, is the SI unit of amount of substance. One mole contains exactly 6.022 140 76 × 1023 elementary entities. This number is the fixed numerical value of the Avogadro constant, NA, when expressed in the unit mol−1 and is called the Avogadro number. The amount of substance, symbol n, of a system is a measure of the number of specified elementary entities. An elementary entity may be an atom, a molecule, an ion, an electron, any other particle or specified group of particles.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
