        <Literal xml:lang="en">The SI unit of pressure. The pascal is the standard pressure unit in the MKS metric system, equal to one newton per square meter or one &quot;kilogram per meter per second per second.&quot; The unit is named for Blaise Pascal (1623-1662), French philosopher and mathematician, who was the first person to use a barometer to measure differences in altitude.

