        <IRI>http://emmo.info/emmo#WattPerSquareMetre</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">&quot;Watt per Square Meter} is a unit of irradiance defined as the power received per area. This is a unit in the category of Energy flux. It is also known as watts per square meter, watt per square metre, watts per square metre, watt/square meter, watt/square metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Watt Per Square Meter (W/m²) has a dimension of MT^{-3&quot; where M is mass, and T is time. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.

-- QUDT</Literal>
