        <Literal xml:lang="en">Dimethyl carbonate is a carbonate ester that is carbonic acid in which both hydrogens are replaced by methyl groups. A flammable, colourless liquid (m.p. 2-4℃, b.p. 90℃) with a characterstic ester-like odour, it is used as a &apos;green&apos; methylating agent and as a solvent. It has a role as a solvent and a reagent.</Literal>
